{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "FULL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 4.0,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-NS-05(ii): record a false-arrival event against driver DRV-01590 on trip TRP-00201 — the 'arrived' marker at 2026-07-23T08:02:14+08:00 was placed while the GPS trace put the driver at least 779.9 m from the pickup pin, and no qualifying in-geofence fix exists anywhere in the trip."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.96,
    "explanation": "The $4.00 cancellation fee cannot stand, and it is refunded in full.\n\nTo the driver (DRV-01590): the finding comes first from your own telemetry. Across all 98 fixes of the trip your vehicle never came closer than 779.9 m to the pickup pin at Blk 118 Rivervale Drive, and there were zero admissible fixes inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius at any point in the 15 minutes before the cancellation. That means POL-NS-01 is not satisfied: limb (b) fails (the trace does not place you in the pickup geofence) and limb (c) fails (in-geofence dwell was 0 seconds against the 300 second minimum). Your 'arrived' marker at 08:02:14 was therefore placed while you were more than 300 m from the pin, so under POL-NS-05 it is a FALSE arrival marker and does not start the waiting clock. Recomputing the clock from the first qualifying in-geofence fix yields no such fix anywhere in the trip, so POL-NS-05(ii) refunds the fee in full, awards no compensation, and directs the false-arrival record that appears in the referrals above. The same result follows independently under POL-NS-02 (no qualifying in-radius fix, so you are deemed never to have arrived) and under POL-NS-06 (0 seconds of effective dwell against the 300 second minimum). The accumulation route in POL-NS-06(i) is unavailable: the traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-00201-01 is MISSING (status MISSING, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT, weight 0.0), so separate intervals could not be summed even if there were any, and the absence is cited for the absence alone. Because POL-NS-01 is not satisfied in full, POL-NS-07 compensation does not arise — the 80% payout presupposes a fully met anchor clause. Your profile does not trip the anti-farming guard (3 no-show terminations in 30 days, 3.1% of 96 completed trips — both below the absolute and rate limbs of POL-NS-07), so nothing is withheld on that ground and POL-NS-09(d) is not engaged; that point is accepted but changes nothing here.\n\nTo the rider: your account is corroborated throughout. Your device stayed within 25 m of the pin on all 122 qualifying fixes, so POL-NS-04 limb (c) is satisfied for the majority (in fact all) of your fixes. Your message at 08:05:33 — 'hello? i dont see any car at 118' — is a locating and coordinating message that both named the block and stated you could not see the vehicle, and the driver neither replied within 120 seconds nor placed an in-app call (trip_record.in_app_calls is empty). POL-NS-04 therefore independently exonerates you and refunds the fee in full, with no driver compensation payable. POL-NS-03 does not rescue the fee either: that clause requires the driver to be stationary outside the arrival radius but within 400 m of the pin, and he was never closer than 779.9 m, so no pin-ambiguity goodwill arises.\n\nAmount: the refund is the $4.00 cancellation-fee line only, which reconciles with the STANDARD zone-class and RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee. No booking or platform fee was charged, so none is refunded. This is a rider-filed dispute and the charge is presently CHARGED with no refund issued, so FULL_REFUND restores the position rather than leaving you with the fee.\n\nNo escalation is warranted: confidence is above the 0.70 floor, the rider and driver have no prior disputes between them, the rider's 30-day no-show dispute count is 0, and the apparent tension between the trip record's arrival marker and the trace is precisely the conflict POL-NS-05 exists to resolve, not an unresolved one. The bundle is unimpaired — the trace has 100% coverage, no gaps and a 10 second cadence, the chat log's 2 messages match trip_record.chat_message_count, and the fare line reconciles — so the confidence cap is set by artifacts of weight 1.0."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "FULL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 4.0,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-NS-05(ii): record trip TRP-00201 as a false-arrival event against driver DRV-01590 — the driver marked 'arrived' at 2026-07-23T08:02:14+08:00 while the trace places him at least 780 m from the pickup pin, and no qualifying in-geofence fix exists anywhere in the trip."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "This dispute is about the S$4.00 no-show cancellation fee charged to the rider, and both briefs are answered together where they make the same point. The charge can stand only if all four conditions of POL-NS-01 hold. The trip record supplies (a) a driver 'arrived' event at 08:02:14 and (d) a driver termination at 08:09:40 under RIDER_NO_SHOW, and the Driver Advocate is right about that — but limbs (b) and (c) fail, as the Driver Advocate itself concedes. Across the driver's own 98 GPS fixes the closest he came to the pin was 779.93 m; there were zero qualifying in-geofence fixes at the STANDARD 50 m arrival radius; and the longest qualifying in-geofence run is 0.0 s against the 300 s minimum dwell. The conjunctive anchor clause therefore fails and the fee is not chargeable. The rider's POL-NS-02 point is accepted: with no qualifying in-radius fix in the 15 minutes before cancellation, the driver is deemed never to have arrived and the fee is refunded in full. POL-NS-03 cannot rescue it — the 400 m wrong-entrance ceiling requires the driver to have been stationary outside the radius but within 400 m, and he was never closer than 779.93 m — so no POL-NS-03(ii) goodwill payment arises. The 'arrived' marker is also a false arrival marker under POL-NS-05: at 08:02:14 the trace puts the driver more than 300 m from the pin. On the POL-NS-05 recomputed basis there is no qualifying in-geofence fix anywhere in the trip, so the fee is refunded in full, no compensation is payable, and the trip must be recorded as a false-arrival event against the driver — that clause-directed instruction is carried in the referrals list. POL-NS-06 independently gives the same full refund: effective in-geofence dwell of 0 s against the 300 s minimum, and the accumulation limb (i) is unavailable because EV-ADVIS-00201-01, the traffic advisory, is MISSING with weight 0.0 — nothing present and populated permits separate intervals to be summed, and there are in any event zero intervals to sum. POL-NS-04 additionally exonerates the rider on all three limbs: (a) the rider's 08:05:33 message named the block and stated he could not see the car; (b) the driver neither replied within 120 seconds nor placed any in-app call (trip_record.in_app_calls is empty); and (c) the rider track keeps the device within the STANDARD 100 m presence radius for all 122 qualifying fixes, maximum deviation 24.9 m. POL-NS-07 compensation does not arise because it operates only where POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full, and POL-NS-04, POL-NS-05 and POL-NS-06 each displace the fee; POL-GEN-03 confirms that on this rider-filed dispute the outcome is a refund of the cancellation-fee line only, not of any booking or platform fee that a completed trip would have attracted. The driver's anti-farming argument is accepted: no_show_terminations_30d is 3 — below the absolute limb of 4 — and 3/96 is 3.1%, below the 0.08 rate limb, so POL-NS-09(d) is not engaged and the profile is not adverse to him. On escalation: no POL-NS-09 trigger fires. The apparent tension between the trip record's arrival marker and the trace is exactly what POL-NS-05 resolves, so limb (b) does not apply; no profile shows 2 or more disputes between these parties (limb (c)); the anti-farming check does not trip and rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d is 0 (limb (d)); and the trace is complete at 100% coverage, no gap over 120 s and a 10 s cadence, while the chat log's 2 messages match trip_record.chat_message_count, so nothing is impaired under POL-NS-08 limbs (a) to (d) (limb (e)). On weight: the deciding facts (the driver's absence and the false marker) are carried by the GPS trace, the trip record and the chat log, all at weight 1.0; the only artifact below 1.0 is the MISSING advisory at 0.0, which carries no fact and is cited solely for its absence — so no discount applies, confidence is not capped below 1.0, and the ruling is comfortably above the 0.70 floor. Result: the S$4.00 cancellation fee is refunded in full to the rider, and no driver compensation is payable."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

{"ruling":{"ruling":"FULL_REFUND","amount_sgd":4.0,"driver_compensation_sgd":null,"referrals":["POL-NS-05(ii): record trip TRP-00201 as a false-arrival event against driver DRV-01590, whose 'arrived' marker at 2026-07-23T08:02:14+08:00 was set while his own GPS trace placed him at least 780 m from the pickup pin and who produced no qualifying in-geofence fix anywhere in the trip."],"confidence":0.95,"explanation":"To the rider: the $4.00 cancellation fee is refunded in full. Your account and the telemetry agree. The driver's own GPS record (98 fixes, 10-second cadence, full coverage of the window) never brings him closer than 779.93 m to Blk 118 Rivervale Drive, and it contains zero in-geofence fixes at the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius. POL-NS-01 only lets the fee stand if all four conditions hold, and limb (b) — the trace placing the driver inside the pickup geofence at or before the 'arrived' event — plainly fails, on the driver's own evidence. POL-NS-02 then gives the refund directly: with no qualifying in-radius fix in the 15 minutes before the 08:09:40 cancellation, the driver is deemed never to have arrived. Three further routes reach the same result: POL-NS-05 makes the 08:02:14 'arrived' marker FALSE (the driver was over 300 m away, in fact over 780 m), and its limb (ii) refunds the fee in full because there is no qualifying in-geofence fix anywhere in the trip; POL-NS-06 refunds the fee for a 300-second shortfall against the 300-second STANDARD minimum dwell (measured dwell: 0 seconds); and POL-NS-04 exonerates you outright, since you sent a locating message at 08:05:33 ('hello? i dont see any car at 118'), the driver neither replied within 120 seconds nor made any in-app call, and your device sat within the 100 m presence radius for all 122 of your fixes. You are refunded the cancellation-fee line only; no booking or platform fee arises on a cancelled trip.

To the driver: the fee cannot stand, and I record that your advocate conceded this — your 98-fix track never reaches the pin, records zero qualifying in-geofence fixes and a longest in-geofence run of 0.0 seconds against a 300-second minimum. That concession against your own interest is accepted, and it is corroborated independently by the trace. POL-NS-03 does not rescue the fee: its 400 m ceiling is the whole test, and you were never within 780 m of the pin, so this is not a wrong-entrance case and no pin-ambiguity goodwill payment arises. POL-NS-07 compensation does not arise either, because it operates only where POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full and no clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displaces it; here limb (b) fails and POL-NS-04, POL-NS-05 and POL-NS-06 each displace the fee. Your profile supports that: the anti-farming guard requires BOTH a count of 4 or more and a rate above 0.08, and you show 3 terminations across 96 completed trips (3.1%), so no farming finding is made against you.

On escalation: this is not an unresolved conflict under POL-NS-09(b). The tension between the trip record's 'arrived' marker and the GPS track is exactly what POL-NS-05 exists to resolve, and POL-NS-05 resolves it against the marker; POL-NS-02 likewise defines arrival by the trace. No profile trigger is met (both counterparty-dispute counters are 0, rider no-show disputes are 0, the anti-farming check does not trip), and nothing in the bundle is impaired under the POL-NS-08 limbs — no clock skew, no sampling gap above 120 seconds, 98 fixes, the chat log's 2 messages match the trip record, and the $4.00 fee reconciles with the greater of the STANDARD zone fee and the RYDE_X tier fee. The one impaired artifact, the MISSING traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-00201-01 (weight 0.0), is cited only for its absence, to confirm that POL-NS-06(i) accumulation is unavailable; it carries no deciding fact and does not depress confidence. Confidence is capped at 1.0 by the deciding artifact, GPS trace EV-GPS-00201 (weight 1.0), and stands at 0.95."},"discarded_claims":[]}
